@startuml
!theme plain
title Active Role and Scope Authorisation
actor User
participant "JWT Middleware" as JWT
participant "Domain Route" as Route
participant "Authorization Service" as Authz
database PostgreSQL as DB

User -> JWT: Request with bearer access token
JWT -> JWT: Validate fixed algorithm, issuer, audience, expiry
JWT -> Route: RequestContext(tenant, user, membership, role, role_assignment)
Route -> Authz: require_permission(code, resource scope)
Authz -> DB: Query selected role_assignment only
note right of DB
Filters include:
- tenant and user
- signed role code
- signed role-assignment ID
- active membership
- validity and revocation
- explicit permission
end note
Authz -> DB: Resolve organisational descendants through closure table
DB --> Authz: allowed / no row
alt permitted
  Authz --> Route: Continue
  Route --> User: Scoped result
else denied
  Authz --> User: 403 active role and scope do not permit action
end
@enduml
